1. Project Overview

The Iris Flower Classification System is a machine-learning application that classifies an iris flower into one of three species based on its flower measurements:

Iris Setosa
Iris Versicolor
Iris Virginica

The system uses four input features:

Sepal Length
Sepal Width
Petal Length
Petal Width

The Java program uses the K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) algorithm to compare a new flower with known training samples and predict its species.